.TH BIGFLOATADD 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatAdd, bigFloatSub, bigFloatMul \- perform signed big float arithmetic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatAdd(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatSub(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatMul(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions store a plus b, a minus b, or a times b in result.
The output may alias either input.  Inputs must be initialized; a distinct
output need not be.  Errors leave the output unchanged.
.PP
Addition aligns mantissas while retaining up to MAX_LIMBS * 32 significant
bits, with guard bits and discarded-tail tracking for subtraction.
Equal signs select addition; different signs select magnitude comparison
and unsigned subtraction.
Subtraction negates a copy of b and calls addition.
.PP
Multiplication computes an exact double-width integer product, combines
signs and exponents, and normalizes the result.  These operations round
toward zero only when the exact result exceeds 8192 significant binary bits.
All exponent calculations use wider integers and check the final range.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success or INT_MAX if the normalized result's exponent cannot
be represented.  Mantissa growth is handled by rounding to capacity.
.SH BUGS
Arithmetic has finite precision and uses rounding toward zero, not to nearest.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatCmpAbs (3),
.BR bigIntMulFFT (3),
.BR bigFloatTruncate (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
